# rdSQL Desktop — local development environment
#
# The open-source build works out of the box with NO configuration here.
# `npm install && npm run tauri dev` runs the full app — every database
# driver (PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, DuckDB, MongoDB, Redis, S3-compatible
# storage) works with zero setup.
#
# The backend URLs (rdsql.com) are hardcoded constants in
# src-tauri/src/commands/backend.rs — not configurable, since the backend
# itself isn't open source or self-hostable from this repo.
#
# The one variable below only matters for the official maintainer release
# build. It's read at COMPILE time via Rust's option_env!(), not at runtime,
# so it must be exported in your shell (or your build tool) before running
# `cargo build` / `npm run tauri build` — a .env file here is not read
# automatically.
#
# Leaving it unset is the normal/default case for anyone building from this
# repo (including forks and PR/branch CI): backend_is_cloud_configured()
# returns false and the app runs fully featured with cloud sign-in, sync,
# and entitlement features simply disabled. This is NOT a real secret —
# see the comment on RDSQL_CLIENT_KEY in backend.rs for why.

RDSQL_CLIENT_KEY=
